text=['# Spectral and Green source review, 03:36 assignment','## Result','All 24 exact assigned hashes received a full static first-to-last read: 75,464 bytes and 2,117 lines. All 24 are new coverage credit after reconciliation against the frozen 1,687-hash inventory, the additive registry, and completed COVERAGE.json artifacts. No supplied source was executed, imported, compiled, syntax-parsed or modified.','This package completes only batches 02_addition_1717_05.json and 02_addition_1717_06.json. It does not declare all materials checked, tests passed, dependency closure reviewed, or the mathematical research solved.','## Most actionable findings','- Custom-modulus Haar uses a square root from the default field (F01).\n- sum_green_matrix fails to pass its modulus to either constituent solve (F02).\n- Both old unittest scripts put additional concrete-Green test classes after unittest.main; direct invocation skips them, discovery includes them (F13).\n- Most certificate acceptance depends on assert, which optimized Python removes (F03).\n- The grid numerical audit has vacuous L=4/8 checks and an overbroad meets_theorem flag (F08).\n- The exact integer spectral certificate has coherent Bareiss/Sylvester logic for its symmetric N>=2 construction; it still needs an input contract and stronger artifact binding (F06/F10).','## Mathematical scope','The one-polynomial-mask K8 spectral obstruction is appropriately restricted and has a coherent multiplicity argument. Explicit conductor and field-descent constructions are finite controls with charged residual costs. The positive two-mask implementation is supported only at N=128/256/512 and does not claim an asymptotic speedup. The parity inverse and two-path/grid/Haar primitives have linear-work applications under their field/pivot assumptions, while their dense audits often cost cubic or quartic work. The halfcut and interval certificates implement the intended contribution rank decompositions; their universal quantifiers come from the underlying structural argument rather than finite shuffle tests.','Finite-field nonzero images can refute compatible characteristic-zero identities when the reduction is valid; one-prime equality is not universal characteristic-zero proof. Floating SVD/eigenvalue/condition reports remain approximate checks. Every source is individually assessed in per_source/.','## Evidence and preservation','COVERAGE.json binds each reviewed hash to its exact source snapshot, full line interval, source-specific review and findings. DEPENDENCY_IDENTITY.json records every local in-batch import plus three outside-scope dependency identities without crediting their bodies. DEDUPLICATION_CHECK.json records frozen/additive/completed-coverage evidence hashes and intersections. PRESERVATION_RECEIPT.json rehashes both every inert code_bytes object and every selected master representative. SHA256SUMS.txt and SEAL.json seal the artifact package.','## Source register']
